    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0398" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/178</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Philip</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 215</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-17">April 17, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reference is made to your despatch No. 527
                    of March 13, last, concerning the negotiation of the new <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Modus Vivendi</hi> between the United States and Chile, and the
                    relationship of these negotiations to a possible commercial agreement between
                    Chile and Great Britain.</p>
                <p>You are authorized to endeavor to ascertain from your British colleague <pb
                        facs="0399" n="389" xml:id="pg389"/> in Santiago, if you perceive no
                    objection, whether the British Government in such an agreement would expect to
                    include an article providing for equality of exchange treatment. You may inform
                    him, in this connection, of the desiderata of this Government in the
                    conversations which you have been conducting with the Foreign Office in regard
                    to a <hi rendition="#italic">Modus Vivendi</hi> between the United States and
                    Chile.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
